##################
## /media requests
##################

### GET all media items
GET {{apiUrl}}/media

### GET 3 latest media items
GET {{apiUrl}}/media?limit=1

### GET media item by id
GET {{apiUrl}}/media/2

### GET media item by id (Not found)
GET {{apiUrl}}/media/0

### Add new media item (JSON, no file included!) / NO TOKEN!
POST {{apiUrl}}/media
content-type: application/json

{
  "filename": "60ac.jpg",
  "title": "New image",
  "description": "The description of the new image",
  "user_id": 305,
  "media_type": "image/jpeg"
}

### Add new media item WITH IMAGE (form-data) WITH TOKEN!
POST {{apiUrl}}/media
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----Boundary

------Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="title"

New cat image
------Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="user_id"

1
------Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="image.png"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./cat900.jpg
------Boundary--


### Add new media item (Bad request, title missing)
POST {{apiUrl}}/media
content-type: application/json

{
  "filename": "60ac.jpg",
  "description": "The description of the new image",
  "user_id": 305,
  "media_type": "image/jpeg"
}

### Modify own media item (200 OK)
PUT {{apiUrl}}/media/5
content-type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

{
  "description": "updated desc",
  "title": "Uus title"
}

### Delete media item 
DELETE {{apiUrl}}/media/1
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

## / USERS REQUESTS

### Update own user info (200 OK)
PUT {{apiUrl}}/users/2
content-type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

{
  "username": "JaneSmith",
  "password": "to-be-hashed-pw2",
  "email": "jane.updated@example.com"
}

### Try to update another user's info (404 Not Found)
PUT {{apiUrl}}/users/1
content-type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

{
  "username": "HackedUser",
  "password": "newpassword",
  "email": "hack@example.com"
}


## Authentication routes

### Post login with normal user
# @name login
POST {{apiUrl}}/auth/login
content-type: application/json

{
  "username": "JaneSmith",
  "password": "to-be-hashed-pw2"
}

### POST login with admin user
# @name login
POST {{apiUrl}}/auth/login
content-type: application/json

{
  "username": "AdminUser",
  "password": "to-be-hashed-pw4"
}

### Get user info
GET {{apiUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}